meta {
  name: Find devices by location
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/devices?locationId={{locationId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  locationId: {{locationId}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Lists all devices assigned anywhere within a specific Location (site), using the `locationId`
  query parameter on the List Devices endpoint.

  **Parameters**
  - `locationId` (query) — the Location ID to filter devices by. Bound to the collection variable
    `{{locationId}}`, which is empty by default — populate it with an ID from "List Location" before
    running this request.

  **Usage**: Handy for a full hardware audit of a single site, e.g. "how many devices are deployed
  at Site1?"

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/devices/list-devices

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
